From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 22:13:41 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 36/46] flashnext cuda: TF_FLASHNEXT_SHARED_SIDE_SPLIT, a split
 shared expert on the side stream with its gather there

With TF_FLASHNEXT_SPLIT_DENSE=1 at --tp 2 (FP8 and NVFP4) the shared expert is cut by rows and runs in line on both
ranks with a BF16 gather. TF_FLASHNEXT_SHARED_SIDE_SPLIT=1 (off by default) forks it onto the side stream on every rank
after y is cleared, beside the routed experts, and joins before the rank sum. The gather is enqueued host-async on the
blocking split, and it is the only collective between fork and join on both ranks, so the ranks issue gather then sum
in the same order; the slot columns written are the same, so the bits are too.

Extends MiaAI-Lab patch 0016's side stream (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-RTX-PRO-6000-TernsorFold 57d815c, MIT) to the split
expert.
